S3 in Amazon AWS stands for:

Amazon Simple Storage Service

👉 S = Simple
👉 3 = Storage Service — the name has three words starting with S.

Amazon S3 is a cloud storage service used to store:

📁 Files
🖼️ Images
🎥 Videos
📄 Documents
💾 Backups
📊 Data for applications

Example: You can upload your website images, project files, or backups to Amazon S3 and access them from your AWS applications.


=========

An S3 Bucket is like a folder/container in the cloud where you store your files.

Simple example

Think of it like this:

Your Computer

📁 My Folder
   ├── photo.jpg
   ├── document.pdf
   └── video.mp4

Amazon S3

🪣 S3 Bucket
   ├── photo.jpg
   ├── document.pdf
   └── video.mp4
Important terms
S3 = Amazon's cloud storage service
Bucket 🪣 = Main container for storing data
Object = Each individual file inside the bucket

Example:

Bucket: my-project-files
│
├── images/logo.png        ← Object
├── documents/report.pdf   ← Object
└── videos/demo.mp4        ← Object

So, Bucket = like a cloud folder/container, and Objects = files stored inside it.

For your deployed projects, an S3 bucket could store images, uploaded files, PDFs, backups, datasets, or static website files.
